            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say to take and to give: ਲੈਣਾ, ਦੇਣਾ. Then Aman bought a book."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: two short pasts",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਲੈਣਾ and ਦੇਣਾ have short pasts of their own: ਲਿਆ, ਦਿੱਤਾ. They agree with the thing, like every past you have met:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਮੈਂ ਪਾਣੀ ਲਿਆ। — maiṁ pāṇī liā. — I took water."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਅਮਨ ਨੇ ਪੈਸਾ ਦਿੱਤਾ। — Aman ne paisā dittā. — Aman gave money."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਮੈਂ ਅਮਨ ਨੂੰ ਕਿਤਾਬ ਦਿੱਤੀ। — maiṁ Aman nūṁ kitāb dittī. — I gave Aman a book."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The one who receives takes ਨੂੰ. CDIAL lists Punjabi dittā, \"given\" (CDIAL 6140)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
